Pakistan's Supreme Court has just ruled  that prime minister Imran Khan violated  the Constitution his allies in  Parliament prevented the opposition from  proceeding with a no-confidence motion  despite the opposition having a majority  Khan then got Parliament dissolved and  called an election Osama bin Javed is  coming up for us right away from  Islamabad so Osama now that that ruling  has come through first tell us how the  Supreme Court reached this decision  well as we speak to you right now the  five-member bench is reading out its  verdict right now after hours and hours  of deliberations it was delayed by half  an hour at least before they were  supposed to announce it but we can tell  you now that the Supreme Court of  Pakistan has declared that it was  unconstitutional for the deputy speaker  of parliament to rule against the vote  of no confidence which means that the  assemblies have been restored the ruling  that the deputy speaker gave throwing  out the vote of no confidence is  enshrined in the Constitution that after  a motion has been tabled before the  assembly that the Prime Minister should  go for a vote of no confidence no other  business can take place and this was The  Plea that was brought forward by the  opposition parties to the Supreme Court  of Pakistan saying the ruling was  unconstitutional the Prime Minister saw  that he's going to lose his numbers as  the motion had been table before  Parliament he could not go back and  dissolve the assemblies and call for  elections so he used the deputy speaker  and his law minister to go through  another route which was unconstitutional  and that is what appears to be the  unanimous decision by this five-member  bench now this is going to have a  wide-ranging ramifications because soon  after that ruling the Prime Minister  wrote to the president the assemblies  were dissolved the PRI the president  actually asked for an interim government  as well and called for elections in 90  days and it appears that in after this  ruling has been declared  unconstitutional all of those subsequent  steps will be rolled back as well  so what is it that happens next what  should we be watching out for  well we've been speaking to leaders of  the opposition people who went to the  Supreme Court and some of the lawyers  who've been pleading their case as well  and they say that the first step is to  get the court to agree that no one  should be able to cite a foreign  conspiracy and strike down uh this vote  of no confidence if the supreme court  allows this then never ever in the  history of Pakistan a prime minister  would be able to vote it out of office  and the next steps would be that now uh  if the court allows them the assembly is  going to reconvene there is going to be  a vote of no confidence the opposition  says that it has more than 172 members  close to a 200 members it says it has  now who say that they do not believe  that Imran Khan should be the prime  minister of Pakistan there is also talk  about elections and that is something  that we saw in the last few days at the  Supreme Court as well uh these questions  arising on how are they going to govern  the country uh when are the elections  going to take place and what will be the  way forward word because you have to  realize that this country now is  polarized between supporters of Imran  Khan and the opponents of Imran Khan and  what this has brought to the fore as  well is the role of Pakistan's powerful  military establishment as well where  Imran Khan the sitting prime minister  for the first time has said that he was  given options by the military  establishment to either resign to  dissolve the assemblies or face the vote  of no confidence and he's found a Fourth  Way Forward and that seems to have been  struck down by the Supreme Court of  Pakistan so it is going to be a an end  to a constitutional crisis but again a  lot of ambiguity on the road ahead  because Pakistan is scheduled to have  elections a year and a half later but if  things are to go by where the opposition  has been calling for elections there has  been calls for a new mandate from the  government as well it appears that  Pakistan is probably going to be heading  towards a new Mandate of fresh elections  where people are going to decide who  they believe should be in power thank  you so much Osama bin Javed reporting  from Islamabad  foreign
 

